      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "The course of asthma is frequently altered by pregnancy, but the mechanisms remain undefined."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "The purpose of this study was to identify specific maternal or pregnancy characteristics that are related to the course of asthma during pregnancy."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "A secondary analysis of a previous prospective study identified 568 pregnant women whose patient-reported asthma course during pregnancy was compared with the women's usual disease course. Potential explanatory variables were compared between groups defined by their pregnancy versus usual course (better, worse, same)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Improvement of asthma during pregnancy was noted in 33.6%, worsening was reported in 36.3%, no change was reported in 26.4%, and the course was uncertain in 3.7%. There was a significant concordance between asthma course and course of rhinitis during pregnancy. Rhinitis improved in 51.1% of patients whose asthma improved during pregnancy and worsened in 19.8% of these women. Rhinitis worsened in 55.9% of patients whose asthma worsened during pregnancy and improved in 2.1% of these women. No significant relationships were found between gestational asthma course and maternal demographic factors, panic-fear score, smoking, maternal weight, infant birth weight, or infant sex."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "The relationship of gestational asthma course to rhinitis symptoms may have clinical and mechanistic significance. Further studies will be necessary to test this hypothesis."
        }
      ]},
